Why this file is separate
-------------------------

GitHub classifies a repository's license by fuzzy-matching the root `LICENSE`
against the SPDX corpus. Appending this notice to `LICENSE` pushed the match
below the detection threshold, so the repository displayed as "Other" instead
of MIT. Keeping `LICENSE` as unmodified SPDX text and the attributions here
lets automated license tooling read the terms correctly while the credit
stays visible to people. Nothing is dropped by the split.
